<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alauddin Khalji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1316">1316</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Alauddin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alauddin Khalji was a sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> who reigned from 1296 until his death in 1316. He repelled Mongol invasions, extended the sultanate's power into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and introduced market price controls and stricter land revenue collection. His reforms made the sultanate one of its most centralised and militarily powerful periods.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji.jpg" alt="Alauddin Khalji" width="320" height="361" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 14th century author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Execution_of_Jalal-al-Din_Firuzshah_II_(r1290-96),_Jami_al-Tawarikh_(Alauddin_Khalji_detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
